            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0360" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1186: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation
                            (Gibson) to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-27T11:00:00+01:00">June 27, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 27—5:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. My telegram No. 278, June 26, 6 p.m. Correspondents at Lausanne were
                    informed from British sources yesterday afternoon of my meeting with MacDonald though no details were revealed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
